  "slug": "telomere-genome-63e9",
  "summary": "Global food and anaerobic digestion metagenome catalogs now sit alongside long-read profiling methods that resolve symbionts and strains.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is reference infrastructure that organizes microbial genomic data by environment or host. PLATE assembles 4,690 food metagenomes into plasmid contig catalogs with host, taxonomy, and AMR/functional annotations, and CAnDi catalogues global anaerobic digestion microbiomes. The remaining preprints are methodological and concern inference on such data. SYMBIO-SCAN applies full-length long-read 16S rRNA sequencing to beetle symbiont detection, validated on a mock community. Sourmash is benchmarked on long-read metagenome mock communities, with gene content recovery F1 of 0.942-0.998. Separately, 550 soil MAG-derived genome-scale metabolic models support FBA predictions of phylogenetically conserved amino acid and fermentation fluxes. Together, these items point to curated catalogs and long-read-compatible profiling feeding functional inference, although this thread is not shared by every item.",
